00:08:04.870 --> 00:08:06.460
And so I want to get to this point.

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:07.601
Give us the context,

00:08:07.601 --> 00:08:10.330
because we are on this kind
of back to school moment,

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:12.710
you've dived, you've gone headfirst

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:14.790
into an initiative for back to school.

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:18.050
Please explain that to the
audience and give some context.

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:18.883
- Great.

00:08:18.883 --> 00:08:21.620
So back in February,

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:23.242
I'm sort of seeing that
the medical community

00:08:23.242 --> 00:08:25.670
was having some issues with messaging

00:08:25.670 --> 00:08:27.310
and struggling on that front.

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:29.310
And I really thought of what Hollywood did

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:30.820
during World War II.

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:32.480
So I reached out to some friends I've had,

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:33.460
who've worked in the government,

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:35.760
going back to the Clinton administration.

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:38.050
These are lifelong public service people.

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:42.390
And I said, "Hey, is there
anything we can do teaming up?"

00:08:42.390 --> 00:08:44.360
And that's, I called John Rogers.

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:48.000
And he reached out to the
CDC with the CDC foundation

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:51.560
and we formed this
partnership with Facts2Health.

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:52.665
And our whole idea was,

00:08:52.665 --> 00:08:55.290
"Hey, let's create a hub for people."

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:57.610
Except instead of just being Hollywood,

00:08:57.610 --> 00:08:59.080
let's unlock the internet

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:01.970
and the artist that is in
everyone around the planet

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:03.320
and their voices.

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:04.890
And we're going to give
you the hard science.

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:07.010
Here's the data, here are the facts,

00:09:07.010 --> 00:09:09.000
no politics, no anything.

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:11.790
This is how we all stay healthy.

00:09:11.790 --> 00:09:13.670
This is how we all stay safe.

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:16.550
And this is how we all
keep as normal a life

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:18.950
in a pandemic world as possible.

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:21.563
Because there are countries
that are killing it right now.

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:25.590
Like Japan, Japan has 2.9% unemployment.

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:27.810
They have 1,200 deaths.

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:30.450
They have no economic shutdown.

00:09:30.450 --> 00:09:34.680
Because as a culture, since
the Spanish influenza in 1918,

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:36.020
they all wear masks.

00:09:36.020 --> 00:09:37.110
Whenever they're feeling sick.

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:40.581
And now everyone has the
potential to infect someone else.

00:09:40.581 --> 00:09:43.150
I don't wear my mask to protect myself.

00:09:43.150 --> 00:09:45.130
That protects me this much.

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:49.260
I wear my mask to protect you,
which protects you that much.

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:50.930
And that is why we wear a mask.

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:53.990
You're not doing it to,
you're not appearing weak.

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:55.080
You're appearing strong.

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:56.375
You know.

00:09:56.375 --> 00:09:58.003
- Tom, you know,

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:00.530
how difficult is it to overcome

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:02.010
